From: tene11 <tene11@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:31:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Keep Cleanroom's LWJGL 3 the only LWJGL in the instance

Cleanroom brings LWJGL 3 as org.lwjgl. If the instance also has the
org.lwjgl3 component, both end up on the classpath and the game crashes
on start with "Incompatible Java and native library versions detected"
(UnsatisfiedLinkError in MemoryUtil.ngetPageSize).

This happens with a Minecraft that was customized by hand to require
org.lwjgl3: resolving the profile keeps adding LWJGL 3 3.3.1 next to
Cleanroom's 3.4.3. Installing Cleanroom now reverts such a Minecraft to
its original version (after asking, as the changes to it are lost) and
removes the org.lwjgl3 component. Other components that require
org.lwjgl3 stop the installation before anything is changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019uQWuLEagQcA1VAuw2GCJd
